---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Zoya Hassan">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 prose prose-invert">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.32em] text-white/60">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-5xl font-light text-white">Zoya Hassan</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-mist/90">
      I am a software engineer moving toward computational astrophysics and scientific software. I already
      know how to design and debug programs; I am building the physics and numerical habits that make
      simulations trustworthy.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-white/60">How I learn</h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-mist/85">
      <li>Read a concept in the textbook.</li>
      <li>Write the governing equations and assumptions.</li>
      <li>Implement a small model in Python.</li>
      <li>Visualize results and compare to theory.</li>
      <li>Ask whether the output makes physical sense.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.28em] text-white/60">Tools</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mist/85">
      Python, NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib, Jupyter, and tests for important numerical behavior. Later: Astropy,
      HPC, and machine learning where the science needs them.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
